      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Shadowspear on turn 2 instead of Nihil Spellbomb against a mill deck. The opponent is playing UB Mill (Flooded Strand, Island, Archive Trap/Glimpse the Unthinkable are typical). Nihil Spellbomb would provide graveyard exile capability which could be crucial against mill strategies and also protects against the opponent potentially using graveyard-based cards. Shadowspear's +1/+1, trample, and lifelink are nice on Nethergoyf, but the equip cost of 2 means it won't be equipped until turn 3 at earliest anyway. Meanwhile, Nihil Spellbomb could sit ready to exile the opponent's graveyard (less relevant) or more importantly be available as an artifact in the graveyard to boost Nethergoyf's power via card types. However, Shadowspear is also an artifact that could end up there. The real consideration is that against a mill deck, having Nihil Spellbomb ready to crack could be important, though it exiles the opponent's graveyard, not yours. Given Nethergoyf cares about YOUR graveyard card types, and the mill opponent will be filling YOUR graveyard, Nihil Spellbomb targeting yourself would be counterproductive. So actually Shadowspear is reasonable - it provides a clock with lifelink to race the mill plan. This is debatable but not clearly wrong.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Shadowspear on turn 2",
      "better_line": "Could have cast Nihil Spellbomb to have ready as a hedge, but Shadowspear to equip Nethergoyf and race with lifelink is a defensible aggressive line against mill.",
