    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "The opponent has Thought-Knot Seer in hand, which is a 4/4 that will exile a card from GPT4om's hand when it enters. Nethergoyf is currently only a 2/3 (artifact and creature in graveyard after Nihil Spellbomb, but only 1 card type - artifact - so it's 1/2, or with Divest adding sorcery to GY it grows). Meanwhile, Thought-Knot Seer is a much more impactful card - it's a 4/4 body AND it exiles a nonland card from GPT4om's hand, which is devastating given the mill player's hand full of key spells like Fractured Sanity, Glimpse the Unthinkable, and Archive Traps. Nethergoyf can also escape from the graveyard later. Discarding TKS would protect the hand and remove a bigger threat.",
