      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player discarded Polluted Delta instead of a less valuable card. With Hedron Crab on the battlefield, fetch lands are extremely powerful - each one triggers Hedron Crab to mill 3 cards. The player already has 3 Archive Traps in hand, and the opponent is about to search their library (Urza's Saga chapter III), which means all 3 Archive Traps can be cast for free. But future fetch lands provide additional mill triggers with Hedron Crab AND can trigger Archive Traps if drawn later. Meanwhile, Fractured Sanity costs UUU which is very difficult to cast with only 1 Island in play and no other blue sources, making it a reasonable discard candidate. Alternatively, one of the three Archive Traps could be discarded since having 3 is redundant when the opponent may not search again after this turn.",
