    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to kill a Hedron Crab with Fatal Push against a mill deck. Two Hedron Crabs double the mill rate (6 cards per land drop vs 3). The reasoning about waiting to destroy an Urza's Saga construct is confused - there's no opposing Urza's Saga. Hedron Crab IS the primary threat engine in the mill matchup and should be removed ASAP.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting any spells, holding Fatal Pushes for a later threat.",
      "better_line": "Cast Fatal Push targeting one of the Hedron Crabs to halve the opponent's mill rate. Could also cast Pithing Needle (naming Polluted Delta or another fetchland to prevent landfall triggers) with remaining mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 56,
      "player": "Gem25P Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 40,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player intended to equip Shadowspear to Nethergoyf (costing {2} for the equip ability), but instead activated Shadowspear's {1} activated ability ('Permanents your opponents control lose hexproof and indestructible until end of turn'), which does nothing useful here since the opponent has no hexproof or indestructible permanents. This wastes 1 mana and fails to equip the Shadowspear. The player's reasoning explicitly states they want to equip, but they selected the wrong ability.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Shadowspear's {1} ability to remove hexproof/indestructible from opponent's permanents (pointless since opponent has none).",
      "better_line": "Activate Shadowspear's Equip {2} ability targeting Nethergoyf to make it a 5/6 with trample and lifelink, creating a dominant threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 67,
      "player": "Gem25P Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 44,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT4om Analyst is a mill deck that needs to discard to hand size. Surgical Extraction can be cast for 2 life (Phyrexian mana) at instant speed and doesn't require mana, making it always castable. However, discarding it isn't terrible since the opponent's graveyard has 5 cards and Surgical Extraction's value is situational. The bigger issue is that Glimpse the Unthinkable requires UB mana and the player only has 1 Island and no black sources on board, making it harder to cast than the other options. Drown in the Loch is the most valuable card to keep as interaction. Archive Trap is free if opponent searches. Fractured Sanity is powerful mill. Surgical Extraction costs 0 mana effectively and could strip key cards like Kozilek's Command or Thought-Knot Seer from the opponent's deck. Discarding Glimpse the Unthinkable (which requires a black source they don't have yet) would have been more reasonable, or one of the redundant Archive Traps since they have 3 copies.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Surgical Extraction to hand size",
      "better_line": "Discard Glimpse the Unthinkable (hardest to cast with current mana base of just 1 Island and no black sources) or a third Archive Trap (redundant with 3 copies, and opponent may not search enough times to use all three for free)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 74,
      "player": "GPT4om Analyst",
      "decision_index": 50,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing a second Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth is illegal or wasteful due to the legendary rule — there's already one on the battlefield. The player will have to sacrifice one of them immediately, effectively wasting their land drop for the turn. Ifnir Deadlands would have been a strictly better land drop, providing colorless or black mana (with Urborg already in play making it a Swamp too) plus a useful activated ability against opposing creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Played a second copy of Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth, triggering the legend rule and losing one to the graveyard.",
