    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Used Drown in the Loch proactively at sorcery speed to destroy Nethergoyf (a 4/5) rather than advancing the mill game plan with Glimpse the Unthinkable. Drown in the Loch is one of their few interactive/reactive spells that can counter spells at instant speed, and spending it proactively wastes that flexibility. Additionally, the opponent can escape Nethergoyf from graveyard later. Meanwhile, Glimpse mills 10 cards which advances the primary win condition and also powers up future Drown in the Lochs and enables Visions of Beyond's draw-3 mode sooner.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Drown in the Loch to destroy Nethergoyf",
      "better_line": "Cast Glimpse the Unthinkable to mill opponent for 10, advancing the mill win condition while saving Drown in the Loch for reactive use (countering important spells or removing threats at instant speed when needed)",
