      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT4om Analyst used Surgical Extraction (paying 2 life, going to 9) to target Divest - a 1-mana sorcery hand disruption spell that is largely irrelevant at this stage of the game. The opponent has already used their discard spells and has a developed board with Thought-Knot Seer. Meanwhile, there are far more impactful targets available: Nethergoyf (which can escape from the graveyard and is a recurring threat), Emperor of Bones (two copies in graveyard, a recursive threat engine), or Urza's Saga (two copies in graveyard, and removing future copies from the opponent's library eliminates a powerful card advantage/tutor engine). Targeting Divest accomplishes almost nothing meaningful while spending 2 life that matters at 11 life against a 19-life opponent with a Thought-Knot Seer on board.",
